  contraband: []
  boothLines:
  - "Buenos d\xEDas, mijo. Ay, you look so skinny. Are they feeding you in this little
    box?"
  - "I'm going to my granddaughter's quincea\xF1era. Fifteen years old! When I was
    fifteen I was already married. Different times. Worse times. But better tamales."
  - Two hundred tamales. Pork, chicken, and rajas. The rajas are for the vegetarian
    boyfriend. Nobody likes him.
  - Here, take one. No? You'll take one. I'll leave it on the counter. You'll eat
    it when I'm gone. I know.
  lineIfApproved: Que Dios te bendiga, mijo. Eat the tamal.
  lineIfRejected: ...Okay. I'll call her. She'll understand.
  lineIfImprisoned: For the TAMALES?! My grandson is a lawyer! ...He's in his first
    semester, but still!
